WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.400
A year of moderate aerobic exercise enlarged the hippocampus by 2% in older adults, offsetting typical

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:15.700
annual shrinkage. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 145. One year of moderate aerobic exercise

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:23.580
produced a 2% increase in hippocampal volume in older adults. The gain offset the typical annual shrinkage

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:29.440
observed in this age group. The finding comes from direct measurement rather than indirect markers.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.760
Researchers tracked brain structure before and after the full intervention period using imaging.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:42.300
Now, shifting to how external exposures can alter cognitive development during adolescence.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:48.740
A longitudinal study followed adolescence who began using cannabis and compared them with nonusers.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:55.180
Memory, attention, language, and processing speed showed slower growth after initiation.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:01.340
Abilities developed normally at first, then plateaued while nonusers continued improving.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:07.820
THC appeared most strongly associated with the memory changes. Investigators planned to follow

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.960
the cohort into early adulthood to assess persistence of the differences.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.960
A randomized trial tested a phone-based adherence app among patients with tuberculosis.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:24.740
Treatment success rose from 74% to 82% while dropout fell by nearly one third.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.560
The app delivered reminders and tracked medication intake in real time.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:35.240
The study was conducted in routine public health clinics rather than specialized centers.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.140
Follow-up work will examine whether similar tools maintain gains when scaled to larger

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:47.820
regional programs. Researchers examined national vital statistics data after Greece introduced

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:55.860
austerity policies in 2010. Infant mortality rose 43% and remained elevated in subsequent years.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.760
The increase was sharpest in the first years of spending cuts.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:06.320
The analysis compared pre and post- austerity trends while controlling for other economic indicators.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.040
Public health researchers will track whether later policy reversals altered the trajectory.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:18.200
Analysis of accident records from England and Wales showed e-scooter riders suffered

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.120
traumatic brain injury at three times the rate of motor cyclists.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:28.640
Riders also sustained more internal organ and vascular damage than either motor cyclists or

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:35.860
pedal cyclists. The study drew on hospital data covering multiple years of rising e-scooter use.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:41.280
Authors note the absence of helmets and higher speeds on shared infrastructure as

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:47.800
contributing factors. Transport safety groups will examine whether design or regulatory changes

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:54.280
reduce the observed excess. On a different note, time-mess stick insects that abandoned sexual

00:02:54.280 --> 00:03:00.280
reproduction roughly one million years ago still carry functional genes required for meiosis.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.500
The finding contradicts the expectation that unused reproductive systems erode rapidly under

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:13.000
relaxed selection. Researchers sequenced multiple species and compared gene content with sexual

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:19.720
relatives. The retained genes showed little evidence of degradation despite the long asexual period.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:26.260
Future work will test whether these genes retain any cryptic function or simply persist by chance.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:33.840
University of Maryland researchers rapidly twisted a microscopic tip to detect infrared-induced flexing

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:40.060
in two-dimensional materials. The approach yields higher spatial resolution than conventional scanning

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:46.700
methods. It captures mechanical responses at the nanoscale without requiring cryogenic conditions.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:53.520
The technique was demonstrated on several atomically thin samples. The group intends to apply it

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:59.460
to other light-responsive layered materials. A study of multiple species showed that water

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:06.300
transport efficiency, not temperature alone, predicts whether trees shift upslope or downslope with warming.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.220
Species with traits that tolerate drier soils move downhill despite rising temperatures.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:19.340
Data came from long-term forest plots across elevation gradients. The results indicate that water

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:26.380
availability can override thermal cues in range shifts. Ecologists will incorporate hydraulic measurements

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:32.720
into future distribution models. Researchers used laser spectroscopy to determine the nuclear

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:39.920
shape of fermium-255 with high precision. The measurement provides the first detailed structure

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:46.240
data for this heavy actinide. The work was performed on samples produced in accelerator facilities.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:52.940
The results refine models of nuclear deformation in the heaviest elements. Additional isotopes

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:59.740
will be examined to map trends across the actinide series. High-resolution imaging revealed internal

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:06.500
structures inside warm clouds that allowed droplet coalescence before ice forms. The observations

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:13.100
address a long-standing gap in understanding precipitation initiation. Data were collected during

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:19.420
targeted aircraft flights through developing cloud systems. The work suggests that certain droplet

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:25.740
size distributions and turbulence patterns suffice to start rainfall. Most people assume rain

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:32.860
begins only when ice crystals form inside clouds and grow heavy enough to fall. Right now, as warm

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:40.300
moist air rises, tiny droplets collide and merge inside turbulent eddies. A single droplet only 50

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:46.040
micrometers across can grow into a rain drop a million times larger in volume through repeated

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:52.660
collisions. Modellers will now test whether these mechanisms improve forecasts of warm rain events

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:59.100
from cloud microphysics to a different measurement challenge. Mapping ice that is already on the ground.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:05.600
A new model produced an updated global map of glacier ice volume using machine learning methods

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:12.100
trained on field measurements. The map improves estimates of stored freshwater and potential sea level

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:18.140
contribution. The study combines satellite imagery with ground observations from multiple continents,

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:24.300
lead researchers at Kaffa Skari University and the Institute of Polar Sciences led the effort.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:30.700
Subsequent versions will incorporate new high-resolution imagery from upcoming satellite missions,

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:37.320
from large-scale environmental sensing to a much smaller-scale sensing problem inside cells and

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:44.080
devices. A levitating micro magnet measured magnetic fields two week for conventional room temperature

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:51.500
sensors. The device operates without liquid helium cooling or heavy shielding. It targets applications

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:57.720
such as brain activity mapping and cardiac monitoring. The prototype achieved sensitivity levels

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:04.560
previously requiring bulky cryogenic setups. Engineering teams plan to miniaturize the system for

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:11.120
portable medical use. Researchers found the same silver nanocatalyst uses different reaction sites

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:17.560
depending on whether the cell generates electricity or produces hydrogen. The discovery supplies a new

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:24.320
design principle for solid oxide cells that perform both functions. The work was carried out on operating

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:30.620
cells at elevated temperatures typical of these devices. The team expects the insight to guide

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:36.860
electrode architecture that improves efficiency in reversible systems. Next measurements will test

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:43.300
whether the site switching behavior holds across other metal nanocatalysts. A new platform uses

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:50.380
reconfigurable optical paths to overcome the lack of natural photon interactions. The design allows

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:57.100
photons to perform a wider range of logic operations than fixed interferometers. prototype devices

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:03.420
demonstrated basic gate operations with measurable fidelity. The architecture was developed to scale

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:09.880
toward fault tolerant photonic processors. Next steps include integrating more modes while maintaining

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:17.300
low loss. Oak Ridge National Laboratory scientists created a method that rapidly identifies genetic elements

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:24.300
controlling microbial chemical production. The platform was tested on bacteria engineered to synthesize

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:30.480
target compounds. It pinpoints regulatory sequences that can be edited to improve yield.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:37.000
The approach supports faster strain development for domestic manufacturing of materials and critical

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:43.760
minerals. Teams will apply the tool to additional host organisms, from detecting faint signals to

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:50.140
another public health intervention that improves detection of treatment gaps. A randomised trial enrolled

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:57.940
257 uninsured Hispanic adults with diabetes and assign them to telehealth coaching plus physician

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:06.560
feedback or usual care. The intervention lowered HBA1C by an additional 1.0 percentage point over 12

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:12.380
months. Community health workers delivered the coaching and relayed glucose data to physicians.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:17.580
The trial took place in primary care settings serving low income populations.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:24.760
Investigators will assess whether the model sustains gains beyond one year. From real-world health

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:30.420
interventions to the final note on measurable mechanisms operating across different timescales.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:36.600
Keep an eye on follow-up data from the adolescent cohort as researchers track whether cognitive

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:43.300
differences persist into early adulthood. That's Planetary and Daily for today. If you enjoyed this,

